socks5: an empty socks_proxy_address means no socks proxy, not a bad one

Since upstream 3e7f041dd ("core-net: C-087: fail vhost creation on a bad
socks proxy address"), lws_create_vhost() fails when
lws_socks5c_ads_server() rejects info->socks_proxy_address.  An empty
string is rejected ("socks_proxy needs to be address:port"), so a vhost
created with socks_proxy_address = "" now fails with "bad socks proxy
address".

Before that commit the error was ignored and "" left the vhost without a
socks proxy, which is the only way an application could say "no socks
proxy" explicitly: NULL makes lws fall back to getenv("socks_proxy"), and
there is no option flag to turn that fallback off.  txiki.js parses the
proxy environment itself (http_proxy / https_proxy / all_proxy / no_proxy)
and pins every client vhost's other proxy kind to "", so with NULL a
socks_proxy in the environment would silently route its direct and
no_proxy connections through a socks proxy.

Treat "" as explicitly disabled: no socks proxy and no env fallback, and
no error.  A non-empty bad address still fails vhost creation as C-087
intends.  The http proxy side already treats "" this way (lws_set_proxy()
on "" leaves the vhost without a proxy, and its error is not fatal).

Not an upstream backport: v5.1.0 (5f39aa483) and main (d954e68f2) both
reject "".  Upstreamable as is.

---
diff --git a/lib/sansio/socks5-client.c b/lib/sansio/socks5-client.c
index 559cad301..0e708c163 100644
--- a/lib/sansio/socks5-client.c
+++ b/lib/sansio/socks5-client.c
@@ -213,6 +213,10 @@ lws_socks5c_ads_server(struct lws_vhost *vh,
 
 	/* socks proxy */
 	if (info->socks_proxy_address) {
+		/* "" means explicitly no socks proxy, and no env fallback */
+		if (!info->socks_proxy_address[0])
+			return 0;
+
 		/* override for backwards compatibility */
 		if (info->socks_proxy_port)
 			vh->socks_proxy_port = info->socks_proxy_port;
